WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.762
Why insist on read scopes?

2
00:00:01.762 --> 00:00:03.700
Look at what the clients actually do.

3
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.899
The drift client reads identities,

4
00:00:05.899 --> 00:00:10.675
uncorrelated accounts and Graph users,
and optionally the directory audit.

5
00:00:10.675 --> 00:00:15.212
The re-read client reads one
account, one identity or one user.

6
00:00:15.212 --> 00:00:17.651
Nothing in Pass 1 writes anywhere.

7
00:00:17.651 --> 00:00:21.654
So a manage scope on either client
buys nothing and risks a lot:

8
00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.088
a stolen token could change accounts.

9
00:00:24.088 --> 00:00:27.010
The workflow scope left
on a standing client lets

10
00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:29.862
anyone add workflows that
call out of SailPoint.

11
00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:34.420
And an administrator's personal token
runs the whole kit as an org admin.
